{
  "id": "ep106",
  "duration": 54.181,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.446,
      "text": "A missing hyphen did not actually destroy NASA's first interplanetary rocket.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner 2 illustration.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner_2_illustration.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.446,
      "end": 12.666,
      "text": "On July 22, 1962, Mariner 1 launched toward Venus aboard an Atlas-Agena rocket.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlas Agena with Mariner 1.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Agena_with_Mariner_1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.433,
          "end": 8.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.467,
          "end": 12.667,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.666,
      "end": 20.166,
      "text": "At 293 seconds, wild steering corrections forced a safety officer to detonate the spacecraft.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Launch of Ranger III with Agena.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Launch_of_Ranger_III_with_Agena.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.667,
          "end": 20.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.166,
      "end": 26.186,
      "text": "Author Arthur C. Clarke and press accounts famously blamed a missing hyphen in guidance code.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASAComputerRoom7090.NARA.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASAComputerRoom7090.NARA.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.167,
          "end": 26.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.186,
      "end": 33.556,
      "text": "In reality, programmers omitted a single mathematical overbar above the letter R in guidance equations.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.2,
          "end": 33.567,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.556,
      "end": 40.401,
      "text": "Without that smoothing bar, the computer treated minor radar noise as violent velocity fluctuations.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Woomera 1964 0(1).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woomera_1964_0(1).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.567,
          "end": 36.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 36.767,
          "end": 40.4,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.401,
      "end": 47.451,
      "text": "That exact code had flown safely on lunar missions, but an in-flight hardware failure triggered the flaw.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Ranger 1 hangar.jpg",
        "credit": "NSSDC Master Catalog Display",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ranger_1_hangar.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.4,
          "end": 47.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.451,
      "end": 53.831,
      "text": "Five weeks later Mariner 2 reached Venus, proving space history's most famous typo was not a hyphen.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner 2 illustration.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner_2_illustration.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.467,
          "end": 54.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
